The version of Colossal Cave Adventure that ran on Honeywell's Phoenix
Multics system in 1980: Don Woods' 350-point game in Gary Palter's
Multics Fortran port, with early material by Dave Platt (rooms,
treasures and creatures later found in his 550-point game), for a
maximum of 462 points. Rebuilt from transcriptions of the surviving
line-printer listings, with the bugs in the code and database fixed and
the unfinished TAKE ALL / DROP ALL completed.
